p3_noop_detail: |
  The original ES4 P3 (2026-06-03) shipped the CalibratedPrediction STRUCT
  but the prediction_calibrated METHOD was never written. The 3 P3 counters
  (outcome_learner_predict, outcome_learner_brier, outcome_learner_cold_start)
  were defined in gate_metrics.rs:696-704 with 0 callsites. The P3 checkpoint
  claimed ✅ SHIPPED; the actual code state was struct-only.
p3_corrective_wave: ES4 P5 (this wave) — added the missing method + wired 3 production consumers
p3_spec_prose_error: |
  The P3 spec_compat_reason I wrote in the P2-P4 closure checkpoint described
  the bucket scheme as "Cold/Low/High by n<10/<30/≥30". The actual code uses
  the existing 4-bucket PredictionConfidence enum (None/Low/Medium/High via
  from_total(0/1-4/5-19/20+)). Fixed in the P5 spec_kb.yaml update.

