# ═══ META-LESSONS ═══
L1: P3 checkpoint claimed "✅ SHIPPED" but the prediction_calibrated METHOD was missing — only the struct existed. FASE 0 cargo check would have caught this if we'd grepped for the method name explicitly. Future: every "✅ SHIPPED" claim must be backed by `grep -n <method_name> crates/`.
L2: When a checkpoint paraphrases enum variants ("Cold/Low/High" vs actual "None/Low/Medium/High"), the spec_kb.yaml inherits the error and oracle scores get misattributed. Future: copy enum variant names EXACTLY from source.
L3: CandidateAction struct changes ripple to every callsite (new(), test helpers, struct literals). For non-trivial struct additions, prefer the builder pattern OR update all sites atomically in one commit.
L4: The CAH oracle is human-curated — bumping spec_compat_prior without changing code is meaningless; changing code without bumping is invisible. Both must be done in the same wave.
L5: 5 atomic counters (P2.3 + P3.2 + P4.2) all need at least one call site to be useful. An orphan counter (defined, never incremented) is dead code. The P3 wave defined 3 counters without wiring any callsite — they were orphan until P5 wired them.
